        "original_id": "119f171f-a56b-5525-add2-44e5a9ac3a9f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Corydalis, Cedrus\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, plant families, native ranges\n\nFacts:\n- Corydalis is a genus of about 470 species of annual and perennial herbaceous plants in the Papaveraceae family.\n- Corydalis is native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere and the high mountains of tropical eastern Africa.\n- The name Corydalis comes from the Greek \"korydalís,\" meaning \"crested lark.\"\n- Cedrus, commonly called cedar in English, is a genus of coniferous trees in the Pinaceae family.",
